# The CI `Format check` gate runs `ruff format --check .` on windows-latest,
# and pyproject.toml pins `[tool.ruff.format] line-ending = "lf"`. Without an
# explicit attribute, a fresh Windows checkout materializes CRLF (git's
# core.autocrlf default on Windows runners), so every file fails the gate --
# a repo-wide failure independent of any milestone's content. Forcing LF in
# the working tree on all platforms makes the checkout match both the index
# (which is already LF) and ruff's configured line-ending.
* text=auto eol=lf
